{
  "_comment": [
    "Single source of truth for anything both Terraform and CI need to know.",
    "Terraform reads it through modules/aws-config; the workflows read it with",
    "jq. Keeping one file means a new account or a changed region is one edit,",
    "not a grep across five stacks and three workflows.",
    "",
    "Account IDs are committed deliberately. They are not credentials — every",
    "role ARN in every trust policy contains one — and CI needs them before it",
    "has assumed anything, so a secret would be circular. The controls that",
    "matter are the OIDC trust conditions and the SCPs, not obscurity. See",
    "docs/decisions/ADR-0004-committed-account-ids.md.",
    "",
    "IDs are empty until bootstrap has run. Fill them with:",
    "  make config-sync",
    "which writes them from the bootstrap stack's outputs.",
    "",
    "contact.phone is empty on purpose. Alternate contacts are where AWS sends",
    "abuse reports and compromise notices; the API requires a phone number, and",
    "a placeholder there looks populated in an audit while reaching nobody in an",
    "incident. Fill it in and re-apply, or leave the contacts unset knowingly."
  ],
